{"context":"EKA has no code awareness: code accessed via raw read/grep (entire files 280-320 LOC, ~9.4k tokens for 5 hits) — file is 5-10x noise vs needed symbol. Research area 6 investigated code context reduction mirroring knowledge context (Finding 6, spk:code-symbol-precision). Minimum useful code context is not file but symbol → signature+40-60 line slice + 1-hop imports/callees → lazy tests/config, not Task→Files→Entire Files. Alternatives evaluated: file-level (LOW reduction), symbol indexing (HIGH, 95% determinism), import graph (highest ROI/cost), AST dump (REJECT for LLM), full call graph (LATER, 60-70% determinism, poor cache/invalidation), semantic RAG/chunk embedding (REJECT as canonical, non-deterministic, hallucination risk; optional plugin only). Prototype measured Go/TS/Python across eka-cli/core/mcp: symbol+1-hop import -72% tokens (-78% refs), -81% noise, p@1 0.33→0.58 (+25pp), p@3 0.58→0.83, success 5/12→8/12; indexing cold 1k files 1.8-2.4s (~2ms/file), incremental 10 files 45-90ms, cache 1.2MB, determinism 98.7%; Python fallback (proximity+test heuristic+grep) lifts p@1 0.25→0.50 with +12% token, without it drops -20pp. Must align with P1 Separation of Concerns / P6 Single Writer / P14 Minimum Canonical Core: code is not authored knowledge and must not be CKO/exchange.","decision":"Code Graph is a DERIVED Runtime cache, not a Canonical Knowledge Object and not an exchange artifact (P1/P6/P14). Implementation:\n\n1. Package eka-core/codegraph (Runtime consumer, like contexts) with tree-sitter per lang (Go/TS/Python first via smacker/go-tree-sitter pure-Go fallback) incremental per file, import graph from import_statement nodes (Go import \"...\", TS import ... from/require, Python import/from), and 1-hop callee via name-match in file scope (no cross-file type resolve for MVP — deterministic \u0026 cheap; full call graph REJECT for MVP).\n\n2. Store ~/.eka/cache/\u003cproject\u003e/codegraph-\u003cgitDigest\u003e.json (gitignore) — derived, rebuilt on eka sync hook diffing fileHash (sha256 per file) → re-parse changed files only; global invalidation per gitDigest (git rev-parse HEAD). Size ~1.2MB per digest, cold 1.8-2.4s, incremental 45-90ms measured. Not in snapshot, not versioned RSF, not a CKO; repo git remains source of truth.\n\n3. Serve via code_context (MCP+CLI) mirroring context semantics: code_context(symbol|file, depth local|dependency|engineering, opts {noContent, compact, limit}) → L0 symbol slice (signature + 40-60L slice, 20±anchor, import block max 10L), L1 deps (imports+1-hop as refs file:line:signature without body), L2 tests (heuristic *_test.go/*.test.ts/test_*.py importing focus, max 8 refs), L3 config lazy. Bounded 32 symbols / 64 units hard cap (same as ADR-021 engineering 64) priority L0\u003eL1\u003eL2, sorted deterministic file:line, --no-content = refs only. Full body via code_get offset/limit with truncated handle (like ToolOutputProcessor pagination). Never send raw AST to LLM.\n\n4. Dynamic langs fallback (MVP mandatory): unresolved imports as string refs (lazy), test linkage heuristic, precision\u003erecall (when miss, don't hallucinate edge), Python grep fallback bounded top 20 tagged role:fallback-grep low confidence. Full LSP type-resolve = LATER (cost high, determinism 60-70%). RAG/semantic search = LATER optional tooling plugin, never canonical.\n\nDeterminism/cache: per fileHash cache valid forever, per gitDigest global; output sorted file:line, first-role-wins dedup; Go/TS/Python MVP first, incremental watch LATER. No migration, no spec bump, no CKO.","consequences":"Positive: token -72% median (-78% refs) and +25pp p@1 measured; incremental 45-90ms allows eka sync hook; fileHash cache validates GO/NO-GO criteria (cut≥50%, p@1 +10pp, incremental \u003c150ms, determinism ≥95% — all met 98.7%); bounded 32/64 prevents context explosion like engineering 64; mirrors knowledge context pattern so agent instruction uniform (dependency --no-content analogue for code). Negative: adds eka-core/codegraph dep (tree-sitter cgo vs pure-Go build tag, tsconfig paths alias resolver heuristic imperfect for MVP), Python fallback +12% token and still 0.50 p@1 (needs LSP later for 0.70+), code index file per digest not shared across machines (rebuild cheap though). No breaking change to existing eka get/context or RSF/CKO model.","alternativesConsidered":"File-level indexing only (fallback) — LOW reduction, kept as fallback when symbol miss. Full AST dump to LLM — token-inefficient, LLM-illegible, kept internal only. Full transitive call graph / pointer analysis for LLM — global expensive, 30-40% incomplete in dynamic langs, poor cache/invalidation; moved to LATER offline batch only, MVP uses 1-hop name-match. Vector DB / embedding chunk RAG as primary — non-deterministic, model-coupled, re-index cost, hallucination risk; REJECT as canonical, allowed as optional code_search plugin in Tooling layer. Code as CKO / docs file / snapshot artifact — violates P1 Separation and P6 Single Writer; REJECT. Cgo vs pure-Go: cgo heavier in CI → pure-Go fallback via build tag. LSP type-resolve for MVP — cost high, determinism 60% → LATER."}